    "q-84098": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84098",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[\\frac{1}{2}X]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=6.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any constant $a$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX]=a\\text{E}[X].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
