    "q-109227": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109227",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[-0.25X].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find $\\text{E}[X].$ \n\nThe expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.1+4\\cdot 0.1+6\\cdot 0.3+8\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-0.25X] & =-0.25\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =-0.25\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
