    "q-109298": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109298",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[-\\frac{3}{2}X-5].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find $\\text{E}[X].$ \n\nThe expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+10\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+15\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-\\frac{3}{2}X-5] & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{E}[X]-5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 10-5 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
